#ASSERT `s 511A(3) the members may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` (JUST TRUE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-12: was #ASSERT `s 511A(3) the members may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE; the function is named for a grant or a power and its plain "if" gate fails, so it now answers NOTHING, not JUST FALSE (name-test sweep of 2026-11-12, fork F16); the text does not say the grant is refused
#ASSERT `s 511A(3) the members may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` (JUST TRUE) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 511A(3) the members may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` (JUST TRUE) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 511A(3) the members may apply to the court for an order removing the auditor` (JUST FALSE) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
