-- The deontic forms run (traces are read, not asserted: see NOTES.md). The event strings are the rules' own.
#TRACE `s 511(2) the company's duty to send a copy of the notice to the auditor` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Auditor, "send a copy of the notice of the intended resolution to the auditor proposed to be removed" AT 2
#TRACE `s 514(3) the company's duty to send a copy of the proposed resolution` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Auditor, "send a copy of the proposed resolution to the person proposed to be appointed and to the outgoing auditor" AT 2
-- s 514(4): a MAY within 14 days: representations on day 14 are in time; a clock run to day 15 with nothing done lapses with no consequence
#TRACE `s 514(4) the outgoing auditor's permission to make representations` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Auditor DOES `Action of a party` OF Auditor, Company, "make written representations on the proposed resolution and request their circulation to members" AT 14
#TRACE `s 514(4) the outgoing auditor's permission to make representations` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 15
#TRACE `s 515(3) the company's duty to send a copy of the notice` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY Company DOES `Action of a party` OF Company, Auditor, "send a copy of the notice of the intended resolution to the person proposed to be appointed and to the outgoing auditor" AT 1
